WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:18.157
Ally raced the diner, determined to not let another fib get out of control.

2
00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:22.738
She had to explain to Ray that there had been a misunderstanding about the surprise party.

3
00:00:23.218 --> 00:00:25.219
But Ray was busy talking on the phone.

4
00:00:25.239 --> 00:00:28.980
"I don't want to interrupt him," Ally thought.

5
00:00:30.624 --> 00:00:33.026
"I'll explain all this later at home."

6
00:00:36.549 --> 00:00:41.033
After she and Barry were done collecting signatures for the petition, Ally headed home.

7
00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:45.216
"Alpha is still mad at me.

8
00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:48.839
I have to talk to her about things too," Ally thought.

9
00:00:53.944 --> 00:00:55.945
In her room she booted Alpha up.

10
00:00:57.687 --> 00:00:59.068
"Hi, Alpha, I'm home."

11
00:00:59.888 --> 00:01:01.229
Alpha made a snorting sound.

12
00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:07.913
"I know you're still mad at me, and I'm really sorry," Ally said.

13
00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:12.695
"The fibs I've told have gotten out of control and caused lots of trouble."

14
00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:15.277
"Humans fib because they can.

15
00:01:15.697 --> 00:01:19.579
They do not possess mind-reading abilities like Astralians," Alpha said.

16
00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:22.261
"Fibs can easily get out of control."

17
00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:25.703
"I know that now," Ally said.

18
00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:30.517
"I thought if no one got hurt, then telling fibs wasn't a bad thing.

19
00:01:31.537 --> 00:01:35.238
But I realize you can't always know who your fibs will hurt."

20
00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:38.639
"Affirmative." Alpha's tone softened.

21
00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:40.359
"It is clear you meant well.

22
00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.241
However, logic dictates you must tell the truth to everyone you have fibbed to."

23
00:01:46.201 --> 00:01:46.841
Ally nodded.

24
00:01:46.861 --> 00:01:50.622
"Let's see Who have I fibbed to?

25
00:01:52.063 --> 00:02:00.815
Kate, Julius, Ray, sort of, and this doesn't even include all the people I've hidden my real identity

26
00:02:00.895 --> 00:02:04.217
from—" "Correction," Alpha interrupted.

27
00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:07.780
"It would be unwise to expose your Astralian identity."

28
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.442
"But isn't pretending to be human a kind of fib?"

29
00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:14.685
"There are some truths that could endanger you.

30
00:02:15.605 --> 00:02:19.348
Some fibs are told out of necessity, but you must choose wisely."

31
00:02:20.309 --> 00:02:22.050
Ally groaned.

32
00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:29.074
"I'm still confused, but maybe that's what Mateo meant when he said some fibs are harmless."

33
00:02:29.094 --> 00:02:35.056
"Affirmative." "Thank you for helping me, Alpha.

34
00:02:35.776 --> 00:02:37.717
Okay, I'm going to do it!

35
00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.078
I'm going to tell the truth to everyone I've fibbed to.

36
00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:46.421
But first I have to bring the letters to Mayor Clark and try to fix this mess with

37
00:02:46.441 --> 00:02:47.441
the soccer field."

38
00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:52.523
Ally was about to put Alpha in her pocket when she noticed she had a voicemail message.

39
00:02:52.543 --> 00:02:56.997
"Oh! Lainie called today," Ally said.

40
00:02:57.017 --> 00:02:59.117
"She finally called me back."

41
00:02:59.697 --> 00:03:00.558
Ally hit Play.

42
00:03:00.578 --> 00:03:02.838
"Hi, Ally.

43
00:03:03.258 --> 00:03:05.819
Please call me back about the P.O.D.

44
00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:07.399
as soon as you can."

45
00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:10.700
"Quick, Alpha," Ally commanded.

46
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.121
"Call Lainie."

47
00:03:12.961 --> 00:03:16.142
The phone rang twice before the call went to Lainie's voicemail.

48
00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:17.842
Ally left a message.

49
00:03:17.862 --> 00:03:19.143
"Hi, Lainie.

50
00:03:19.463 --> 00:03:20.703
I'm sorry I missed your call.

51
00:03:21.143 --> 00:03:23.444
Please call me back as soon as you can.

52
00:03:24.252 --> 00:03:26.553
I'm so excited to blast off with you!"

53
00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.614
Ally hung up and got ready to head into town.

54
00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:34.115
"It's time to get back to work!"

55
00:03:34.135 --> 00:03:36.676
Ally arrived at the mayor's office a little while later.

56
00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:39.377
"May I please speak with the mayor?"

57
00:03:39.757 --> 00:03:41.237
Ally asked the mayor's assistant.

58
00:03:41.257 --> 00:03:44.678
"She's in a meeting," the assistant said.

59
00:03:44.698 --> 00:03:47.159
"I can wait," Ally said.

60
00:03:47.179 --> 00:03:49.480
"It's very important."

61
00:03:54.024 --> 00:03:57.105
Ally waited for almost an hour before the mayor's door opened.

62
00:03:58.845 --> 00:04:01.806
Mayor Clark walked out with two men carrying blueprints.

63
00:04:01.826 --> 00:04:04.467
"We're excited for you to get to work!"

64
00:04:04.887 --> 00:04:05.707
she said to the men.

65
00:04:06.387 --> 00:04:08.508
The men handed her the blueprints and left.

66
00:04:08.528 --> 00:04:11.089
"Wait!" Ally jumped up.

67
00:04:11.109 --> 00:04:14.430
"Were you talking about the parking lot?

68
00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.631
Because we collected a lot of letters and signatures on a petition.

69
00:04:19.151 --> 00:04:21.351
Lots of people want to save the soccer field."

70
00:04:21.371 --> 00:04:23.112
"I know.

71
00:04:23.628 --> 00:04:26.349
We're getting a lot of phone calls in support of the field.

72
00:04:27.349 --> 00:04:29.810
But I'm sorry, Ally, it's too late."

73
00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:31.730
Mayor Clark shook her head.

74
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:35.471
"But the kids will lose their soccer field!"

75
00:04:35.871 --> 00:04:36.391
Ally said.

76
00:04:37.312 --> 00:04:38.572
The mayor shrugged sadly.

77
00:04:38.592 --> 00:04:40.573
"It's life, I suppose."

78
00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:45.014
She turned to go back to her office when Ally's eyes landed on the blueprints.

79
00:04:45.034 --> 00:04:48.415
"Are those the plans for the parking lot?"

80
00:04:48.835 --> 00:04:49.315
she asked.

81
00:04:49.335 --> 00:04:51.175
"May I look at them?"

82
00:04:52.436 --> 00:04:53.416
"I don't see why not."

83
00:04:55.468 --> 00:04:57.649
The mayor spread the blueprints out on a table.

84
00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.410
"Here's the parking lot.

85
00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.493
And we've planned for a small drive-through coffee shop so people can grab a cup of coffee on

86
00:05:04.513 --> 00:05:05.253
their way to work.

87
00:05:06.074 --> 00:05:08.235
I was going to ask Ray if he'd like to run it."

88
00:05:09.296 --> 00:05:10.556
Ally's eyes went wide.

89
00:05:11.097 --> 00:05:13.078
She had just gotten the best idea!

90
00:05:13.098 --> 00:05:16.720
"Mayor, did you know that Ray has a food truck?

91
00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:21.562
What if he agreed to serve coffee and breakfast foods every morning?

92
00:05:22.683 --> 00:05:27.765
Then you won't have to build the shop, and the parking lot could be smaller, leaving room for

93
00:05:27.805 --> 00:05:28.406
a field."

94
00:05:29.526 --> 00:05:30.326
The mayor frowned.

95
00:05:31.427 --> 00:05:32.347
Ally held her breath.

96
00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.808
"Please, please, please," she thought.

97
00:05:34.828 --> 00:05:39.610
"You know The mayor looked thoughtful.

98
00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.571
"That's not a bad idea."

99
00:05:46.453 --> 00:05:47.713
She rolled up the blueprints.

100
00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:51.175
"Maybe I'll speak to the developers to see what they think.

101
00:05:52.035 --> 00:05:53.956
Do you want to speak with Ray about the coffee?"

102
00:05:54.996 --> 00:05:55.537
"Of course!"

103
00:05:56.198 --> 00:05:58.360
Ally left the office and crossed her fingers.

104
00:05:58.861 --> 00:06:00.623
But it wasn't because she had told a fib.

105
00:06:01.304 --> 00:06:03.967
This time it was for luck that her plan would work!
